# TryHackMe – Data Encoding

## 📌 Lab Overview
This repository documents my hands-on learning and practical experience with data encoding techniques through the TryHackMe platform.

The lab focuses on understanding how data is represented, encoded, and decoded using different encoding methods commonly encountered in cybersecurity and penetration testing.

## 🎯 Objectives
- Understand the fundamentals of data encoding.
- Identify different encoding formats.
- Practice encoding and decoding data.
- Recognize encoded strings during security investigations.
- Develop practical skills in analyzing encoded information.

## 🛠️ Topics Covered
- Base64 Encoding
- Hexadecimal Encoding
- Binary Representation
- ASCII Encoding
- URL Encoding
- Data Decoding Techniques

## 🔬 Practical Learning
During this lab, I explored different encoding methods and practiced identifying and decoding encoded data.

**Key Takeaways:**
- Encoding transforms data into a different representation.
- Encoding is not the same as encryption or hashing.
- Encoded information can often be decoded without a secret key.
- Understanding encoding is useful when analyzing suspicious strings, web traffic, and captured data.

